---
layout: base
title: Sky Almanac
description: "Every day of the Marducian year under Solara, Nystara, Miras, Toris and Keltas."
permalink: /almanac/
---

<div class="page-header">
  <div class="container">
    <h1 class="page-title">Sky Almanac</h1>
    <p class="page-lead">Every day of the year under Solara, Nystara, Miras, Toris and Keltas. Pick a day to read its sky.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="almanac">

  <div class="alm-yearbar">
    <label class="alm-yearbar__label" for="alm-year">Year</label>
    <button type="button" class="map-btn" id="alm-prev-year" aria-label="Previous year">&lsaquo;</button>
    <input id="alm-year" class="alm-yearbar__input" type="number" min="0" max="9999" value="439" inputmode="numeric">
    <button type="button" class="map-btn" id="alm-next-year" aria-label="Next year">&rsaquo;</button>
    <span class="alm-yearbar__era">MC</span>
    <p class="alm-status sr-only" id="alm-status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></p>
  </div>

  {# The ribbon is one tab stop with arrow-key movement inside it, rather than 386
     separate ones. Same pattern as the relationship graph, and equally invisible
     unless we say so. #}
  <p class="alm-hint" id="alm-keys">
    Tab to the year ribbon, then use the arrow keys to move a day at a time and
    Home or End to jump to the ends of the year. Every day in the month grids
    below is also a button.
  </p>

  <p class="alm-hint">
    This page reads the year. To see a single sky &mdash; where the suns and moons
    actually stand at a given hour, and the two shadows a post casts at that
    moment &mdash; open <a href="/almanac/sky/" class="wikilink">Sky over Ahvantir</a>.
  </p>

  <section class="alm-ribbon-wrap" aria-labelledby="alm-ribbon-head">
    <h2 class="sr-only" id="alm-ribbon-head">Year ribbon</h2>
    <div class="alm-ribbon-scroll">
      <svg class="alm-ribbon" id="alm-ribbon" tabindex="0" role="application"
           aria-describedby="alm-keys" aria-label="Moon phases and sun separation across the year"></svg>
    </div>
    <ul class="alm-legend" role="list">
      <li><i class="alm-sw" data-moon="miras" aria-hidden="true"></i>Miras &middot; 24 days</li>
      <li><i class="alm-sw" data-moon="toris" aria-hidden="true"></i>Toris &middot; 43 days</li>
      <li><i class="alm-sw" data-moon="keltas" aria-hidden="true"></i>Keltas &middot; 66 days</li>
      <li><i class="alm-sw alm-sw--suns" aria-hidden="true"></i>Distance between the suns</li>
      <li><i class="alm-sw alm-sw--two" aria-hidden="true"></i>Two moons full</li>
      <li><i class="alm-sw alm-sw--three" aria-hidden="true"></i>All three full</li>
      <li><i class="alm-sw alm-sw--dark" aria-hidden="true"></i>All three new</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <div class="alm-split">
    <section class="alm-panel" aria-labelledby="alm-day-head">
      <div class="alm-dayhead">
        <p class="alm-eyebrow" id="alm-day-eyebrow">Selected day</p>
        <h2 class="alm-dayhead__title" id="alm-day-head"></h2>
        <p class="alm-dayhead__sub" id="alm-day-sub"></p>
      </div>
      <div id="alm-moons"></div>
      <div class="alm-suns">
        <p class="alm-eyebrow">Solara and Nystara</p>
        <div class="alm-sepbar"><i id="alm-sepfill"></i></div>
        <p id="alm-suntext"></p>
        <p class="alm-note">The suns close once a year. How close rides a rhythm of about eight years, counted from the deep Pairing of 0&nbsp;MC.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="alm-daynav">
        <button type="button" class="map-btn" id="alm-prev-day">&lsaquo; Previous day</button>
        <button type="button" class="map-btn" id="alm-next-day">Next day &rsaquo;</button>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="alm-panel" id="alm-events" aria-labelledby="alm-events-head">
      <h2 class="sr-only" id="alm-events-head">Notable skies this year</h2>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="alm-months-wrap" aria-labelledby="alm-months-head">
    <p class="alm-eyebrow">Nine months &middot; two days outside the Turn &middot; eight-day Turn</p>
    <h2 id="alm-months-head">The Months</h2>
    <div class="alm-months" id="alm-months"></div>
  </section>

  <section class="alm-notes" aria-labelledby="alm-notes-head">
    <p class="alm-eyebrow">Sources and rulings</p>
    <h2 id="alm-notes-head">Calendar notes</h2>
    <p>Months, weekdays and moon phases follow the Marducian calendar as configured in the Ahvantir Foundry world. All three moons begin new on 1 Varenthal, Year&nbsp;1, so the phases here match the table's own moon widget.</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Month lengths.</strong> Six months of 43 days and three of 42, plus two days outside the Turn, for 386. Every year opens on Solkir.</li>
      <li><strong>The drift.</strong> The two days outside the Turn were once the equinoxes, Equinara and Umbrivale. The calendar has drifted, so they keep their places and now carry names fit for where they fall: Cindrafel at the turn from summer heat to harvest, Noctharis at the bottom of winter.</li>
      <li><strong>Era.</strong> Years are counted in the Marducian Calendar, abbreviated MC.</li>
      <li><strong>The Pairing.</strong> Nyhexus circles both suns once a year, so the pair closes and opens once a year too. What varies is how close: a deep Pairing comes round about every eight years, and the count runs from the one recorded in 0&nbsp;MC. When a deep Pairing falls on one of the two days a year the planet crosses the suns' own orbital plane, one sun passes in front of the other.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="alm-note">Phase windows follow the Foundry phase-length tables: Miras 3 days per phase; Toris 6/5/6/5/6/5/6/4; Keltas 8 days per phase with a 10-day waning crescent. See <a href="/articles/marducian-calendar/" class="wikilink">Marducian Calendar</a> and <a href="/articles/solara-and-nystara/" class="wikilink">Solara and Nystara</a>.</p>
  </section>

</div>

